/**
 * INVOICE COLOURS — MTC-FCS-004.
 * ============================================================================
 * Eight palettes, applied to whichever layout is chosen — exactly like the
 * colour themes in the website builder. `primary` carries the logo block, the
 * party names and the total bar; `ink` is the near-black of the bands and the
 * table head; `surface` is the faint tint behind panels.
 *
 * `onPrimary` is the text colour that actually reads ON `primary`. It is
 * declared per palette rather than computed, because only one of the eight
 * needs dark text and a wrong guess is a contrast failure printed on somebody's
 * invoice.
 *
 * `accent` is a second, warmer colour used sparingly — meta labels and the
 * figures in a stats strip — by the designs that have a place for one. It is
 * deliberately NOT used for table body text: a whole column of amber numbers
 * is harder to read, and this is a document about money.
 *
 * ── WHY COLOUR AND LAYOUT ARE SEPARATE ─────────────────────────────────────
 * They were one list to begin with, which meant picking "Cinema" changed the
 * shape of the page as well as its colour and there was no way to have a red
 * invoice in the standard layout. Splitting them makes both choices real:
 * eight colours times the layouts in data/invoice-layouts.js, rather than
 * eight fixed combinations.
 *
 * Every `primary` carries white text at the sizes the designs use it, and
 * every `ink` is dark enough for white text on a solid band.
 */

